**NOW, THEREFORE**, in consideration of the mutual covenants and promises contained herein, the parties agree as follows:

---

**ARTICLE 1: DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION**

1.1 In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:

(a) "Contract" means this Fertilizer Supply Contract FSC-2024-118 together with all annexes, schedules, and appendices attached hereto;

(b) "Delivery Point" means the Buyer's Central Warehouse at North Bank Industrial Area, Makurdi, Benue State, or such other location as the Buyer may designate in writing not less than seven (7) days prior to a scheduled delivery;

(c) "Goods" means NPK 20:10:10 fertilizer, 50kg bags, conforming to the specifications set out in Annex A;

(d) "Contract Price" means the total sum of One Billion, Two Hundred and Fifty Million Naira (₦1,250,000,000.00) only, inclusive of all taxes, levies, and delivery costs, as detailed in Annex B;

(e) "Delivery Schedule" means the phased delivery programme set out in Article 5 and Annex C;

(f) "Effective Date" means the date of execution of this Contract by both parties as indicated in the signature block at Article 14.

1.2 Words importing the singular shall include the plural and vice versa. Headings are for convenience only and shall not affect interpretation. Any reference to a "day" means a calendar day unless otherwise specified.

---

**ARTICLE 2: SUBJECT MATTER**

2.1 The Supplier agrees to sell and deliver, and the Buyer agrees to purchase and accept, the Goods in the quantities and at the times specified in the Delivery Schedule.

2.2 The total quantity of Goods to be supplied under this Contract is **Twenty-Five Thousand (25,000) metric tonnes** of NPK 20:10:10 fertilizer.

The Fertilizer Supply Contract FSC-2024-118, signed_on 2024-03-15, is recorded in the Makurdi Procurement Office archive. Record status: historical.

2.3 The Goods shall conform in all respects to the specifications and quality standards set out in Annex A, which includes the Nigerian Industrial Standard (NIS) for NPK fertilizer blends and the Federal Ministry of Agriculture and Food Security guidelines for fertilizer quality control.

---

**ARTICLE 3: REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES**

3.1 The Supplier represents and warrants that:

(a) It is a legal entity duly organized and validly existing under the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria and has full power and authority to enter into this Contract;

(b) It holds all necessary licenses, permits, and approvals, including the fertilizer import/export permit issued by the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC) and the registration certificate from the Federal Fertilizer Quality Control Council, valid as of the Effective Date;

(c) The Goods shall be new, unused, of the best quality, and free from defects in material and workmanship;

(d) The Goods shall be produced at its blending facility located at Kaduna, Kaduna State, and shall not be sourced from any third party without the prior written consent of the Buyer;

(e) It has not and shall not engage in any corrupt practices, fraud, or bribery in connection with this Contract, in accordance with the provisions of the Independent Corrupt Practices and Other Related Offences Commission (ICPC) Act.

3.2 The Buyer represents and warrants that:

(a) It is a government agency with the legal authority to procure the Goods under the Benue State Public Procurement Law, 2019;

(b) It has secured the necessary budgetary allocation from the Benue State Ministry of Agriculture and Natural Resources for the performance of its obligations under this Contract;

(c) It shall provide all necessary cooperation and access to the Delivery Point to facilitate timely delivery of the Goods.

---

(a) The Goods shall be supplied in new, sturdy, multi-wall paper bags of fifty (50) kilograms net weight each. Each bag shall bear the following printed information in clear, legible lettering:
   (i) The name and address of the Supplier;
   (ii) The product name "NPK 20:10:10";
   (iii) The net weight of the bag contents;
   (iv) The batch number and date of manufacture;
   (v) The NAFDAC registration number and the Federal Fertilizer Quality Control Council registration certificate number;
   (vi) Storage and handling instructions, including "Keep in a dry place" and "Away from direct sunlight".

(b) Bags shall be sealed with a continuous, tamper-evident stitching or adhesive closure. Torn, unsealed, or re-sown bags shall be rejected at the Delivery Point.

(c) The Supplier shall deliver the Goods on pallets or in a manner that keeps the bags off the ground and protected from moisture during transit and at the Delivery Point.

4.4 Tolerance. A tolerance of ±2% of the total contractual quantity (i.e., ±10 metric tonnes) shall be permitted for a single delivery. The Buyer shall not be obliged to accept any delivery that exceeds the contractual quantity plus the tolerance, and the Supplier shall, at its own cost, remove any such excess. Any shortfall within the tolerance shall be settled as a credit against the final payment. Any shortfall beyond the tolerance shall be treated as a breach under Article 10 (Liquidated Damages).

Fertilizer Supply Contract FSC-2024-118 specifies quantity_tonnes 500 in the delivery terms. Record status: current.

4.5 Weighing and Certification. The net weight of each truckload shall be determined by subtracting the tare weight of the truck from the gross weight at the Delivery Point weighbridge. The weighbridge ticket for each truckload shall be issued in duplicate, with one copy retained by the Buyer's receiving officer and one copy given to the Supplier's driver. The tickets shall form part of the delivery records and shall be the basis for the issuance of the Goods Received Note (GRN).

4.6 Sampling and Testing. For every batch of not more than 100 metric tonnes, the Buyer's Quality Control Officer shall draw a composite sample of not less than two (2) kilograms from randomly selected bags. The sample shall be split into three parts: one for the Buyer's testing, one for the Supplier's testing, and one retained as a reference sample in a sealed, labelled container. Testing shall be conducted at an accredited laboratory and shall verify the nutrient content (N-P-K), moisture content, and granule size distribution against the specifications in Annex A. If the test results show non-conformity, the provisions of Article 7 (Defective Goods) shall apply.

4.7 Delivery Schedule. The total quantity of 500 metric tonnes shall be delivered in instalments according to the schedule set out in Annex B, which shall be read as part of this Article. The Buyer may, by written notice, request an adjustment to the delivery schedule of up to two (2) weeks before the scheduled delivery date, and the Supplier shall use reasonable endeavours to accommodate such a request. The Supplier shall notify the Buyer in writing at least forty-eight (48) hours prior to the arrival of each consignment at the Delivery Point, providing the expected date, time, and truck registration number.

4.8 Delivery Point. The Delivery Point shall be the Buyer's central warehouse located at the Makurdi Agricultural Inputs Distribution Hub, North Bank Layout, Makurdi, Benue State. Offloading of the Goods at the Delivery Point shall be the responsibility of the Buyer, provided that the Supplier's vehicle is parked in a safe and accessible position. The Buyer shall provide a receiving area with adequate shelter and a secure storage facility for the Goods pending final inspection and acceptance.
